-- תקנון שירות עובדי הוראה, פרק 1ב', §1.45 בחירות ותעמולה
-- The Attorney General's guidelines on elections and propaganda as the
-- takanon restates them: no public money or public property for election
-- propaganda, no propaganda in state schools, the rules on posters and
-- signs, the penalties the Elections (Propaganda) Law sets, and to whom
-- questions and breaches go.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT common

§ `1.45 בחירות ותעמולה`

-- akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_45__hc_2 The section's title line ("the Attorney General's guidelines on elections and propaganda").
-- akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_45__hc_2/p1 An introduction: the provisions below follow Attorney General's guideline 21.776 of 1 July 1984.

DECLARE `1.45 party` IS ONE OF
    `a takanon party` HAS `who` IS A Party
    `a public body`
    `any person`
    `the chair of the Central Elections Committee`
    `the Ministry's legal adviser`

DECLARE `kind of public body` IS ONE OF
    `a government ministry`
    `a state enterprise or institution`
    `a non-contractual holder, manager or supervisor of state property`
    `a local authority`
    `a corporation the Government takes part in managing or owns capital in`
    `another body`

DECLARE `kind of election` IS ONE OF
    `Knesset elections`
    `municipal or local-council elections`
    `elections of mayors or council heads`

DECLARE `use of public property` IS ONE OF
    `buildings for propaganda lectures, meetings or gatherings`
    `telephones, post or office equipment`
    `notice boards`
    `vehicles`
    `renting or lending equipment`
    `renting buildings or land` HAS `normally for rent` IS A BOOLEAN, `discriminates between parties` IS A BOOLEAN
    `another use for election propaganda` @desc 9 gives examples only; 8 forbids any use

DECLARE `notice or sign` IS ONE OF `a notice`, `a sign`

DECLARE `propaganda act` IS ONE OF
    `use public money for election propaganda`
    `publish material serving election propaganda`
    `use public property for election propaganda` HAS `use` IS A `use of public property`, `placed at a minister's disposal` IS A BOOLEAN
    `conduct election propaganda in a state school`
    `invite a Knesset candidate to talk at a school before Knesset elections`
    `invite to a school someone likely to propagandise`
    `post election propaganda on places meant for the public` HAS `posted item` IS A `notice or sign`
    `post or write on another's property without the owner's consent` HAS `item on property` IS A `notice or sign`
    `remove or deface a lawfully posted election notice` HAS `removed item` IS A `notice or sign`
    `refer the question to the Ministry's legal adviser`
    `issue an order stopping the offence`
    `handle the breach urgently and report to the legal adviser`

DECLARE `consequence` IS ONE OF
    `an offence: six months' imprisonment or a fine`
    `the holder is liable unless he proves he did not know or took reasonable steps`
    `a disciplinary offence for a public servant`
    `the offence of defacing land`
    `the Central Elections Committee chair may order it stopped`

§§ `1-2 Scope`

@ref akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_45__hc_2__para_1
GIVEN e IS A `kind of election`, `the provision of the law applies to local elections` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the provision applies to the election` e `the provision of the law applies to local elections` IF
    e EQUALS `Knesset elections` OR `the provision of the law applies to local elections`

@ref akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_45__hc_2__para_2
GIVEN e IS A `kind of election`, `a question of applicability arises` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `1.45 party` `propaganda act`
DECIDE `local-election questions go to the legal adviser` e `a question of applicability arises` IS
    IF `a question of applicability arises` AND NOT e EQUALS `Knesset elections`
    THEN PARTY `a takanon party` `the Ministry of Education`
         MUST  `refer the question to the Ministry's legal adviser`
         LEST  BREACH BY `a takanon party` `the Ministry of Education` BECAUSE "1.45 section 2: a question whether a provision applies to local elections goes to the Ministry's legal adviser"
    ELSE FULFILLED

§§ `3-6 Public money`

-- 3 and its quotation of section 2א of the Elections (Propaganda) Law: no
-- money of an audited body (section 9(1)-(4) of the State Comptroller Law)
-- or of a corporation the Government manages or owns capital in is used in
-- connection with election propaganda.
@ref akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_45__hc_2__para_3 akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_45__hc_2__para_3/p2
GIVETH A DEONTIC `1.45 party` `propaganda act`
DECIDE `no public money for propaganda` IS
    PARTY `any person`
    SHANT `use public money for election propaganda`
    LEST  BREACH BY `any person` BECAUSE "1.45 section 3 (Elections (Propaganda) Law section 2א): public money is not used for election propaganda"

-- 4: the bodies of section 9 of the State Comptroller Law the prohibition
-- binds. Section 9 calls them "public bodies".
@ref akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_45__hc_2__para_4
GIVEN b IS A `kind of public body`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a body section 4 lists` b IF
    elem b `the bodies section 4 lists`

`the bodies section 4 lists` MEANS
    LIST
        @ref akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_45__hc_2__para_4__subpara_a
        `a government ministry`,
        @ref akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_45__hc_2__para_4__subpara_b
        `a state enterprise or institution`,
        @ref akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_45__hc_2__para_4__subpara_c
        `a non-contractual holder, manager or supervisor of state property`,
        @ref akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_45__hc_2__para_4__subpara_d
        `a local authority`

@ref akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_45__hc_2__para_5 akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_45__hc_2__para_5__subpara_a akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_45__hc_2__para_5__subpara_b
GIVEN a IS A `propaganda act`
GIVETH A LIST OF `consequence`
DECIDE `consequences of misusing public money` a IS
    IF a EQUALS `use public money for election propaganda`
    THEN LIST `an offence: six months' imprisonment or a fine`,
              `the Central Elections Committee chair may order it stopped`
    ELSE EMPTY

GIVETH A DEONTIC `1.45 party` `propaganda act`
DECIDE `the chair may stop the offence` IS
    PARTY `the chair of the Central Elections Committee`
    MAY   `issue an order stopping the offence`

-- 6 (section 17א): whoever held or was in charge of the money or property is
-- liable too, unless he proves the offence was committed without his
-- knowledge or that he took reasonable steps to prevent it.
@ref akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_45__hc_2__para_6
GIVEN `held or was in charge of the money or property` IS A BOOLEAN
      `proved it was without his knowledge` IS A BOOLEAN
      `proved he took reasonable steps` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the holder is criminally liable` `held or was in charge of the money or property` `proved it was without his knowledge` `proved he took reasonable steps` IF
        `held or was in charge of the money or property`
    AND NOT `proved it was without his knowledge`
    AND NOT `proved he took reasonable steps`

§§ `7 Publications`

-- 7: a government ministry, a state enterprise or institution, or a
-- corporation the Government manages or owns capital in, issues no booklet
-- or other material that — from its timing, context, content and wording
-- together, judged by its plain meaning to any reasonable person — serves
-- election propaganda; in an election campaign that includes summaries of
-- activity glorifying a candidate and his list at public expense.
@ref akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_45__hc_2__para_7
DECLARE `publication` HAS
    `its timing, context, content and wording show it serves election propaganda` IS A BOOLEAN @desc judged by its plain meaning to any reasonable person
    `glorifies a candidate's record`    IS A BOOLEAN @desc a summary of activity praising a candidate and his list, during an election campaign

GIVEN p IS A `publication`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the publication serves election propaganda` p IF
        p's `its timing, context, content and wording show it serves election propaganda`
    OR  p's `glorifies a candidate's record`

GIVEN b IS A `kind of public body`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a publisher 7 names` b IF
       b EQUALS `a government ministry`
    OR b EQUALS `a state enterprise or institution`
    OR b EQUALS `a corporation the Government takes part in managing or owns capital in`

GIVEN b IS A `kind of public body`
GIVETH A DEONTIC `1.45 party` `propaganda act`
DECIDE `no propaganda publications` b IS
    IF `a publisher 7 names` b
    THEN PARTY `a public body`
         SHANT `publish material serving election propaganda`
         LEST  BREACH BY `a public body` BECAUSE "1.45 section 7: a public body publishes nothing that serves election propaganda"
    ELSE FULFILLED

§§ `8-11 Public property`

-- 8 (section 2א of the law): public property is not used for election
-- propaganda.
@ref akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_45__hc_2__para_8
GIVETH A DEONTIC `1.45 party` `propaganda act`
DECIDE `no propaganda use of public property` IS
    PARTY `any person`
    SHANT `use public property for election propaganda` u minister
          PROVIDED `a forbidden use of public property` u minister
    LEST  BREACH BY `any person` BECAUSE "1.45 sections 8-10: public property is not used for election propaganda"

-- 9: examples of the ban on using the land or movables of the bodies of 4
-- ("public bodies"). 9ו: halls and open public places normally for rent may
-- be rented, without discrimination between parties.
@ref akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_45__hc_2__para_9
GIVEN u IS A `use of public property`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `forbidden whatever the property` u IF
    CONSIDER u
    @ref akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_45__hc_2__para_9__subpara_a
    WHEN `buildings for propaganda lectures, meetings or gatherings` THEN TRUE
    @ref akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_45__hc_2__para_9__subpara_b
    WHEN `telephones, post or office equipment` THEN TRUE
    @ref akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_45__hc_2__para_9__subpara_c
    WHEN `notice boards` THEN TRUE
    @ref akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_45__hc_2__para_9__subpara_d
    WHEN `vehicles` THEN TRUE
    @ref akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_45__hc_2__para_9__subpara_e
    WHEN `renting or lending equipment` THEN TRUE
    @ref akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_45__hc_2__para_9__subpara_f
    WHEN `renting buildings or land` forRent discriminates THEN (NOT forRent) OR discriminates
    WHEN `another use for election propaganda` THEN TRUE

-- 10: the bans of 9 do not apply to property the state placed at a
-- minister's or deputy minister's disposal.
@ref akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_45__hc_2__para_10
GIVEN u IS A `use of public property`, `placed at a minister's disposal` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a forbidden use of public property` u `placed at a minister's disposal` IF
    (NOT `placed at a minister's disposal`) AND `forbidden whatever the property` u

@ref akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_45__hc_2__para_11
GIVEN `a public servant` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A LIST OF `consequence`
DECIDE `consequences of misusing public property` `a public servant` IS
    IF `a public servant`
    THEN LIST `an offence: six months' imprisonment or a fine`,
              `the holder is liable unless he proves he did not know or took reasonable steps`,
              `a disciplinary offence for a public servant`
    ELSE LIST `an offence: six months' imprisonment or a fine`,
              `the holder is liable unless he proves he did not know or took reasonable steps`

§§ `12-13 Schools`

-- 12: no election propaganda in a state school, by teachers or invited
-- speakers; before Knesset elections no candidate is invited to talk, and
-- at any time no one likely to propagandise.
@ref akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_45__hc_2__para_12
GIVEN p IS A Party @desc the school principal or a teacher (13 names both)
      `before Knesset elections` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `1.45 party` `propaganda act`
DECIDE `no propaganda in state schools` p `before Knesset elections` IS
    PARTY `a takanon party` p
    SHANT a PROVIDED `forbidden in a state school` a `before Knesset elections`
    LEST  BREACH BY `a takanon party` p BECAUSE "1.45 section 12: no election propaganda in a state school"

GIVEN a IS A `propaganda act`, `before Knesset elections` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `forbidden in a state school` a `before Knesset elections` IF
        a EQUALS `conduct election propaganda in a state school`
    OR  a EQUALS `invite to a school someone likely to propagandise`
    OR  (a EQUALS `invite a Knesset candidate to talk at a school before Knesset elections` AND `before Knesset elections`)

-- 13: a principal or teacher who invites, or allows, such a talk risks a
-- criminal trial (section 17: six months or a fine) and disciplinary
-- proceedings before the state or local-authority disciplinary court.
@ref akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_45__hc_2__para_13
GIVEN `invited or allowed a forbidden talk` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A LIST OF `consequence`
DECIDE `consequences for the school` `invited or allowed a forbidden talk` IS
    IF `invited or allowed a forbidden talk`
    THEN LIST `an offence: six months' imprisonment or a fine`, `a disciplinary offence for a public servant`
    ELSE EMPTY

§§ `14-17 Notices and signs`

@ref akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_45__hc_2__para_14
GIVETH A DEONTIC `1.45 party` `propaganda act`
DECIDE `no propaganda on public places` IS
    PARTY `any person`
    SHANT `post election propaganda on places meant for the public` item
    LEST  BREACH BY `any person` BECAUSE "1.45 section 14 (section 9(ב) of the law): no election notices, signs or slogans on buildings, fences, roads, pavements or other public areas"

-- 15: posting or writing on another's property without the owner's consent
-- is the offence of defacing land (Penal Law section 196); whoever ordered
-- the printing or the posting is liable too.
@ref akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_45__hc_2__para_15
GIVETH A DEONTIC `1.45 party` `propaganda act`
DECIDE `no posting on another's property` IS
    PARTY `any person`
    SHANT `post or write on another's property without the owner's consent` item
    LEST  BREACH BY `any person` BECAUSE "1.45 section 15: defacing another's property with election notices (Penal Law section 196)"

GIVEN `posted it` IS A BOOLEAN, `ordered it printed or posted` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `liable for defacing` `posted it` `ordered it printed or posted` IF
    `posted it` OR `ordered it printed or posted`

@ref akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_45__hc_2__para_16
GIVETH A DEONTIC `1.45 party` `propaganda act`
DECIDE `no removing lawful notices` IS
    PARTY `any person`
    SHANT `remove or deface a lawfully posted election notice` item
    LEST  BREACH BY `any person` BECAUSE "1.45 section 16: removing or defacing a lawful election notice is an offence"

-- 17: "the restrictions on notices under sections 15 to 17 above apply to
-- signs too". The range names 17 itself, which restricts nothing, and leaves
-- out 14, the very rule against posting notices (F-1.45-a). Read as 14-16:
-- every restriction above applies to signs, which the prohibitions do by
-- taking a `notice or sign` and binding both.
@ref akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_45__hc_2__para_17
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a clause restricting notices` n IF
    n AT LEAST 14 AND n AT MOST 16

`the clauses 17 cites` MEANS range 15 17

`17 cites itself and leaves out 14` MEANS
        elem 17 `the clauses 17 cites`
    AND NOT `a clause restricting notices` 17
    AND NOT elem 14 `the clauses 17 cites`
    AND `a clause restricting notices` 14
#ASSERT `17 cites itself and leaves out 14`

§§ `18-21 Status and handling`

-- 18: these provisions are for study only; the binding rules are those of
-- the laws. Where the two differ, the law governs.
@ref akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_45__hc_2__para_18
GIVEN `what the guideline says` IS A BOOLEAN, `what the law says` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the binding answer` `what the guideline says` `what the law says` IS
    `what the law says`

@ref akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_45__hc_2__para_19
GIVEN `a Ministry employee whose powers a provision touches has a question, or breached it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `1.45 party` `propaganda act`
DECIDE `questions and complaints to the legal adviser` `a Ministry employee whose powers a provision touches has a question, or breached it` IS
    IF `a Ministry employee whose powers a provision touches has a question, or breached it`
    THEN PARTY `a takanon party` `the Ministry of Education`
         MUST  `refer the question to the Ministry's legal adviser`
         LEST  BREACH BY `a takanon party` `the Ministry of Education` BECAUSE "1.45 section 19: the question or complaint goes to the Ministry's legal adviser"
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- 20: every breach is handled urgently and the handling reported to the
-- legal adviser. "Urgently" sets no number; time in days, with the urgency
-- an input.
@ref akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_45__hc_2__para_20
GIVEN `days that count as urgent` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `1.45 party` `propaganda act`
DECIDE `handling a breach` `days that count as urgent` IS
    PARTY `a takanon party` `the Ministry of Education`
    MUST  `handle the breach urgently and report to the legal adviser`
    WITHIN `days that count as urgent`
    LEST  BREACH BY `a takanon party` `the Ministry of Education` BECAUSE "1.45 section 20: breaches of the propaganda rules are handled urgently and reported"

@ref akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_45__hc_2__para_21
GIVEN `employed by a government company or a state-controlled corporation` IS A BOOLEAN, `its legal adviser is the Ministry's` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `these provisions apply, with the necessary changes` `employed by a government company or a state-controlled corporation` `its legal adviser is the Ministry's` IF
    `employed by a government company or a state-controlled corporation` AND `its legal adviser is the Ministry's`

-- akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_45__hc_3 The heading of the source list (אסמכתא).
-- akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_45__hc_3/p1 A source: director-general's circular מט/1, section 4.

-- Worked examples.
#ASSERT `a body section 4 lists` `a local authority`
#ASSERT NOT `a publisher 7 names` `a local authority`
#ASSERT NOT `a forbidden use of public property` (`renting buildings or land` TRUE FALSE) FALSE
#ASSERT `a forbidden use of public property` (`renting buildings or land` TRUE TRUE) FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `a forbidden use of public property` `vehicles` TRUE
#ASSERT `forbidden in a state school` `invite a Knesset candidate to talk at a school before Knesset elections` TRUE

#TRACE `no propaganda use of public property` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `any person` DOES `use public property for election propaganda` `notice boards` FALSE AT 3
#TRACE `no propaganda use of public property` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `any person` DOES `use public property for election propaganda` `vehicles` TRUE AT 3
#TRACE `handling a breach` 3 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `a takanon party` `the Ministry of Education` DOES `handle the breach urgently and report to the legal adviser` AT 2
